WEBVTT

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.480
Why me?!

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.060
You said that you'd help.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.460
Yeah, give up already, Ooshima.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.720
Don't even try to back out now, Ooshima.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:15.110
Non-chan will support you in every way she can!

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.410
I'm here for you too, Yuuki-senpai.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.120
Yuu-kun, I think you're the perfect man for the job.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.830
Not you too, Mii-chan!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.880
I'm not cut out to be a Student Council President!

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.710
Right? Don't you agree, Morishita-san?

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.750
Normal.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.130
So it's unanimous, huh? I had no clue you were so popular, Yuu-kun.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.040
More like they're just dumping the hard work on me.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.540
The club president orders you, Oojima Yuuki!

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.270
Run in the Student Council presidential election to save the Food Research Club!

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.660
What?!

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.520
Do it.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.040
Congratulations on your marriage!

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.920
They're beautiful! Thank you.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.660
Next time, you'll be the one coming to our wedding!

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.900
Yes, of course!

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:33.880
Make sure you come!

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.840
I see you two are in love.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.550
"Love"?

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:44.820
Yeah. You'll understand it when you grow up a little more.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:48.180
So when the love between you ripens...

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:55.920
Back then, I didn't really know what love was.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.660
And you do now?

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:58.920
I still don't know.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.860
Even though it's so close?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.260
It's not close. I can't reach it.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.980
It's there. You just have to reach out. Try it!

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.140
What... are you doing?!

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:19.880
I should be asking you that.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.080
What are you doing? Pervert!

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.600
I should be asking you that too.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.920
So it's true that people respond when you answer their sleep-talking.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.960
Huh? Did I say something?

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.860
You sure did.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.340
"I love you so much, Chisato!"

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:38.900
"I won't let you go!"

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.240
Don't lie!

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.560
What's your problem?!

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.560
I'm trying to find the person I'm destined to be with, so don't get in my way.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.700
What are you talking about?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.080
Reality is too tough, so I'll settle on finding nice girls in the world of dreams.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.340
Cut the nonsense and wake up already!

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.660
It's Sunday, but we still have a club meeting!

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.760
We need to prepare for the election, too!

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.340
I ain't going to no club.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:02.840
What?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.880
I'm quitting the Food Club,

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.780
and hence I am not running for the election, either.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:07.560
That will be all!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.680
What?!

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.400
This is the Finance Commissioner's manifesto?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.400
The Food Research Club is...

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:22.480
Oh, it's right there at the top of the list.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.220
So our only way out is for Ooshima to become the Student Council President and reject the bill, right?

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.320
He said that he's not going to.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:28.780
Huh?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.180
He said that he's quitting the Food Club.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.440
What?!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.480
Jeez, they always push everything onto me.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.670
There's no way someone like me would get elected—

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.010
Coming through!

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.430
Oh, Ooshima-kun!

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:47.820
Long time no see.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.620
Oh, Matsuri-san!

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.280
See you!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.780
Wait, Matsuri-chan!

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.000
Oh, Oojima-kun, long time no see!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.600
Oh, Ayumu-san!

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.100
Long time no see, Ooshima!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.440
Oops, I meant, Oojima.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.190
Okay.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.020
I finally run into some girls, and it's Ayumu-san's group of all people.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:10.870
So close!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.790
Well, it's not like people bump into pretty girls that oft—

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:20.640
Ouch...

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.120
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.100
Are you all right—

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:29.100
You're the Finance Commissioner.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.840
I'm so sorry. Are you sure you aren't hurt?

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.300
Yes, I should be fine.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.200
Really, I'm so sorry.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.860
You don't have to be so apologetic.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.360
Huh?

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:46.860
I'm at fault, too, since I was riding at a speed in which it was difficult to stop.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.490
Don't you agree, Ooshima-kun?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.660
Huh? How do you know my name?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.560
Here, you dropped these.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.540
Oh, this!

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.870
Right, I need to get this to the academy quickly.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.020
I'm really sorry.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.220
You apologized again.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:03.060
Eh? Oh, sorry!

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.180
Um, I mean... well...

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:09.840
The value of your apologies drop if you say sorry too often!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.610
Use them efficiently.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.350
Okay, Ooshima-kun?

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.680
I understand!

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.600
Then I'll make this my last one.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.810
I am sincerely sorry.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:23.700
I am sincerely sorry, as well.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.320
Um...

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.500
Can I clarify one thing?

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.330
What is it?

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.580
I'm Oojima, not Ooshima.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.200
Oh, please excuse me.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.120
I'm sorry.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.210
This is important, so one more time.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.590
It's Jima. Ji-ma.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.550
Ji-ma, right? I got it.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:50.180
I'm honored you understand.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.500
You're a funny person.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.360
See you.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.100
Yuuki-senpai is quitting? What is this about?

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.620
Why didn't you stop him?

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:03.980
Well, that's because...

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.030
All right.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:07.820
I'll convince him.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:08.940
We're counting on you.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.740
Yes, hello?

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.100
Were you just flirting with me for fun?

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.580
My body's not enough for you now?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.000
What are you talking about?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.210
Senpai, please calm down and listen.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:27.840
The truth is, there's proof of our love in my belly.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.360
You know...

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.240
Don't you want to see our cute baby, Yuuki-senp—

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:36.580
It didn't work!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.100
You didn't even try to begin with.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:41.960
Sheesh.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.760
Let's see...

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.860
All right, I'm counting on you.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.340
You're...

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.340
Oh, we met yesterday!

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.360
I'm glad I found you.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.370
Isn't this yours?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.100
Oh, yes!

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:57.990
Where did you find it?

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.840
I picked it up after we bumped into each other.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:03.000
I figured it belonged to you.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.840
Thank you very much.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.040
This is the key to my house.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.800
You saved me the trouble of replacing the lock.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.360
I'm glad to hear that.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:13.720
I guess it was worth coming here in a hurry.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.800
You came here for this even though it's Sunday?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.310
Oh, no. I have a club meeting to attend.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.940
<i>Though I said that I was quitting this morning.</i>

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.120
Which club?

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.960
It's called the Food Research Club.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.590
All we do is eat snacks, though.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:31.200
That sounds fun!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.490
Do you have a club meeting, too?

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:33.980
Oh, no.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:36.910
You see, I'm a financial aid student, so...

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:41.660
<i>Shoot. School regulations prohibit financial aid students from joining clubs.</i>

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.260
I have to work at the factory today.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:49.630
I gotta go! Um, I'll thank you properly for this another time.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.900
Don't worry about it.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.120
You should hurry!

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.590
Right! See you, then!

00:08:56.270 --> 00:09:00.100
U-Um, if you don't mind, could you tell me your name?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.280
I'm Oojima Yuuki, a second-year.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.960
Oojima-senpai, huh?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.480
I'm Aomi Isara, a first-year. See you later!

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:11.360
Isara-chan, huh?

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:16.760
Yuu-chan's quitting the Food Club? That's too much for me to take!

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.360
Non-chan, could it be that you...

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.410
...had a thing for Ooshima?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:23.160
Non-chan will die without Yuu-chan!

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.960
Is it <i>that</i> bad?!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.840
I set the photo we took together as my wallpaper.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.000
Oh, show me!

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:35.300
This is...

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.300
an Oojima Roll?

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:43.930
If Yuu-chan quits, where will I get his handmade special, the Oojima Roll?!

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:48.760
Come back, Oojima Roll!

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:56.380
I'm coming across a lot of pretty girls today.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:10:00.740
Maybe my luck for chance encounters is looking up!

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.200
Oh, another one!

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.000
My apologies. I seem to have bumped—

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:09.840
Who are you?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:11.860
Are you from General Affairs? Or the Finance Commission?

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:12.800
Answer me!

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.480
What is this about?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.150
College prep program second-year, Ooshima Yuuki.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.640
Food Research Club.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.900
It's not Ooshima. It's Oojima!

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:22.560
Ouch!

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.120
Stay put!

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.320
Let him go, you two.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.520
But President...

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:29.820
President?

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:41.040
Just let him go.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:41.700
But...

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:47.420
I doubt anyone is out to get me when so little time remains in my term of office.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:48.210
Understood.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.660
Forgive us for the violent treatment.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.400
Due to the nature of my job, I must be prepared for many possibilities.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.760
Even for the possibility of violence, huh?

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.360
I really wouldn't be able to handle it.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:08.340
Oh, are you running in the presidential election?

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.780
No, I'm not.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.310
I just have people around me telling me to.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:15.320
To save the Food Research Club from being forced to disband, right?

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:16.980
How did you know?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.460
I read the list in Candidate Shinonome's manifesto, and Ooshima-kun...

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:25.380
Excuse me, Oojima-kun, your Food Research Club was on the list of clubs to disband,

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.540
so I figured that could be why.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.240
You're exactly right.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.910
You still won't run?

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:33.420
There's no way someone like me would get elected.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.320
But that means the club will be disbanded.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.620
I suppose that'd be fine, too.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:40.470
That's mean!

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.500
You could at least show some sympathy!

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.810
You've misunderstood. What I was referring to was...

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:49.180
You running in the presidential election, Oojima-kun.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.840
You should vote for a candidate you agree with.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:56.060
If there isn't one, you should become a candidate yourself.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.920
It's a very natural choice.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:58.650
But—

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:02.160
The Public Safety Commission will refrain
from entering a candidate this year,

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.030
leaving only two likely candidates.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.600
Don't you think this is a good chance?

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:09.720
You have my support.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.660
Farewell.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:19.630
Jeez, what's Yuuki thinking? How could he disobey me, the club president?

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:26.220
I think the best solution would be for you to make up with Yuu-kun and bring him back.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.780
You're making it sound like we broke up.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:31.680
What's wrong, Michiru?

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.690
You don't like chocolate flavor?

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:38.440
I can't really eat it.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.380
You can have them.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:42.110
Blue.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.560
Huh? Blue?

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.870
You like blueberry flavor?

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:46.920
This is fine.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.120
We need to think of something else.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.400
Hey, how about working on achievements now so we won't have to disband?

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:58.220
It's not that easy to create achievements.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.460
My new creation!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:06.120
Reverse spin prevention mechanism-equipped hyper tornado-shaped extra long impact mixer with aero!

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:06.720
Or for short...

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:08.980
...Nero-Nero Machine?

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.560
Yes, it's the sixth version!

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:13.080
Would that count as an achievement?

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.390
I made it even more powerful!

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:19.440
Fold... Fold...

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.860
Fold it to death... yay!

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:28.980
A perfect Neroneronerone with zero coarseness should be complete!

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:32.750
This is the dream of all Nero-ers!

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:34.660
There is little doubt that the Finance Commissioner will

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:39.130
reconsider her decision to disband our club when she sees this wonderful machine!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.500
Now, let's see this in action!

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.500
Non-chan, isn't that a bit too much?

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.550
All right, switch on!

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.680
She went and pressed it.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.520
The club will disband if I don't run, huh?

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.650
But I gotta win, too.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:08.910
That's...

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.130
What's the matter?

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:14.620
Oh, we meet again, Bowjima-kun.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.330
Bowjima? I'm Oojima.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:22.300
You seemed to consider the "jima" part important,

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.020
so I figured it'd be okay to not care about the rest!

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:25.360
It's not okay!

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.840
What do you mean by, "Bow" anyway?

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:31.120
You kept bowing the whole time, so I thought it would fit.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:31.850
Was I wrong?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.120
Yes, you were!

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:36.020
That aside, is something wrong?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.100
The chain came off.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.600
This is a problem.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.760
I have a ton of stuff to do today.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.020
Let me see it.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:45.540
I think I can fix this.

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:53.740
There we go.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.040
It's fixed.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.660
Your hand got dirty.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.040
Clean it with this.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.100
But then your handkerchief will get dirty.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.100
Just use it.

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:06.550
Thank you.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.260
I should be the one saying thanks.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.180
I appreciate the help.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.220
I see.

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:15.980
A candidate from the Food Research Club.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:18.100
It's unreasonable, to say the least.

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.320
I don't think it's unreasonable.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:22.480
It could be worth a try.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.100
Not you too, Shinonome-san.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.240
Um, can I ask you something?

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:28.610
What is it?

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:32.360
Why do you intend to disband the Food Club?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:40.330
Close friends get together and eat snacks at the cafeteria with some tea.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:45.080
How does the Food Research Club differ from that?

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:48.700
How is that a club activity?

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.000
I don't think it qualifies as a club.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.600
That's why I intend to have it disbanded.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.220
Is there something wrong with my reasoning?

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.120
No, you aren't really wrong.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.320
You say it so easily.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.660
You're not even devoted to the club.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:05.860
That's not true!

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:10.660
It's not just me. Everyone in the Food Club loves it and wants to keep it alive!

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:11.460
So...

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:12.150
So what?

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:18.540
So we thought we'd fight in the election instead of just sitting and waiting for it to die.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.040
And? Are you going to run?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.400
No, we're just being desperate.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.300
There's no chance of us winning.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.420
Then here's a question for you.

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:33.090
What do you call the horses that win derbies?

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:37.260
I'd call them... "the strongest horses," I guess.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.970
That's not wrong, but that's not the answer I had in mind, either.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.900
What's the answer?

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:46.480
They're the horses that entered the derbie.

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:49.120
That much is obvious.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:53.580
But I think horses that don't enter derbies never have a shot at winning one.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.540
The same applies to elections.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:00.740
The probability of someone who doesn't enter the race not winning is 100%.

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:03.620
And one more thing...

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:09.630
I personally like seeing people put up a fight even when they know they won't win.

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:11.590
Shinonome-san...

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.340
I should get going now. Later.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:18.960
Now I made you listen to my story even though you're so busy. I'm sor—

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:20.850
I mean, thank you!

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:26.120
I was going to call you Bowjima again, but it seems like I missed my chance.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.320
<i>Only the horses that enter the derby can win.</i>

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.760
<i>The horses that don't enter can never win.</i>

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.380
Oojima's here.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.220
Welcome back, Oojima Roll!

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:50.760
Thank goodness you didn't break up with Chisato.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.160
You were worried about our child, weren't you?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.260
That's wonderful.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:55.880
Welcome back, Papa!

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:00.140
Um, what the hell is going on?

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:03.260
We're covered in Neroneronerone because you didn't come.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.810
So this is <i>my</i> fault?

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:10.660
I had some time to think,

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.960
and I decided to fight for the Food Club!

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:17.950
However! Since I've decided to run, I want to really try to win.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:23.080
I don't want to do this just because you're halfheartedly forcing pesky tasks on me.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.020
Do you have something in mind?

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.960
How about an intra-club election?

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.360
An intra-club election?

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:29.880
Yeah.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:35.630
Everyone should vote for who they think has the highest chance of winning the presidential election!

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:38.130
I see! That's a pretty good way to do it.

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.320
I'm up for it.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.280
Really?

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:45.520
Yep! It's fair, simple, and reasonable.

00:18:46.030 --> 00:18:47.220
What do you guys think?

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.630
Agreed!

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:49.730
Me too.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.690
Let's see...

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.960
When we're actually voting...

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.500
...it's not easy to decide.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:07.750
Guys, before you write down your vote, I want you to listen to what I have to say.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.250
Thinking back, the Food Club has been pretty damn laid back.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.130
All we've done is eat snacks obtained using our club funds and chat.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:21.890
I'm sure others would think of us as useless, lazy, spoiled, and unproductive all around.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:26.010
Maybe it's really no surprise that we're on the list of clubs that should disband.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:32.020
But it's through the Food Club that I came to meet all of you.

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:34.520
You were here whenever I came,

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:39.400
and we would laugh and mess around. It was really fun.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:43.140
No matter what anyone else says, this is an important place for me.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.700
I don't want to lose it.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.720
So I want you guys to take this very seriously

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.240
as you think about the person who would have the best chance.

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:54.030
Someone that all of us would want to support.

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:54.920
Stare.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:57.740
What is it?

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:01.440
Leadership is a requirement.

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:03.540
So is courage.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:06.960
So is decisiveness when making a choice.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:10.720
So is the likability that makes everyone want to support you.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.860
Of course, appearance is also important!

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:18.070
Everyone, please vote for someone who can really win the election.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:19.720
I'm counting on you.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.240
<i>Well, that should do it.</i>

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:27.910
I see, I see.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:33.170
And thus, Oojima Yuuki has been elected!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.960
Hooray!

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:35.860
Hooray.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:38.670
I don't understand what just happened.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.630
Wait! Didn't you guys listen to my speech?!

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:45.280
I thought you'd all choose Chisato!

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:45.890
Why?

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:50.940
Wow! I never thought I'd be moved by a speech from Ooshima.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:52.770
Your speech was great, Ooshima!

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:55.600
It convinced me that you'd do well if you run.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.770
It earned Non-chan's endorsement, too!

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.150
You were so cool that I almost came.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.040
Huh?

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:02.980
Oojima.

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:03.450
Yes?

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.540
Good luck.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.080
I-I dug my own grave!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:13.220
You're just gonna have to humbly accept the result of this fair election!

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:13.920
Fine.

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:16.540
See you later!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.540
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:23.300
See, you should've just done as I told you.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.200
I wouldn't have been convinced that way.

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.580
No grumbling!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:29.000
You're my property, after all!

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:32.680
You know, Chisato, I'm not your property or...

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:38.100
Hey.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:41.980
How about one?

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:56.840
Is it good?

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:58.240
Yeah.

00:21:58.870 --> 00:21:59.630
That's good.

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:45.660
You know how the "you" in <i>youkan</i> uses a character for "sheep"?

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:46.940
Yeah, you're right.

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:52.700
Apparently, that's because it was created when people
imitated a lamb dish with beans a long time ago.

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:56.840
Oh, like how <i>nikujaga</i> was created as an imitation of beef stew?

00:23:56.840 --> 00:23:59.000
I can see how that came about,

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:02.180
but I wonder what the original lamb dish that <i>youkan</i> imitated is.

00:24:02.180 --> 00:24:04.580
Well, that's, um...

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:07.320
Next time, Episode 3: "Strategy."

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:11.100
Since there's the "kan," maybe Genghis Khan?
